      <section class="section">
        <h2>What Sunriver Is Known For</h2>
        <p>
          Sunriver is known for family-friendly vacations, bike paths, resort amenities,
          golf, vacation rentals, and easy access to the Deschutes River. It is one of
          the most popular places in Central Oregon for families who want an easy base
          with plenty to do without needing to plan every minute.
        </p>

        <p>
          It is also popular because it works in every season. Summer is the busiest,
          but winter trips, spring breaks, fall weekends, and holiday stays all bring
          people to Sunriver.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Things To Do in Sunriver by Season</h2>

        <div class="grid">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Spring</h3>
            <p>
              Good for quieter bike rides, family trips, golf when weather allows, and
              easier access before the summer rush.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Summer</h3>
            <p>
              Peak season for biking, pools, river days, golf, vacation rentals, family
              activities, and trips toward the Cascade Lakes.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Fall</h3>
            <p>
              Quieter weekends, cooler bike rides, golf, scenic drives, and relaxed
              family trips after peak season.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Winter</h3>
            <p>
              Cozy vacation rentals, trips to Mt. Bachelor, holiday stays, winter walks,
              and indoor family activities.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Family Trips</h3>
            <p>
              Sunriver is especially useful for families because many activities are close
              together and easy to repeat across a multi-day trip.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Bike Path Days</h3>
            <p>
              The bike paths are a major part of the Sunriver experience and one of the
              easiest ways to explore without constantly driving.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Food, Coffee, and Easy Vacation Meals</h2>
        <p>
          Sunriver’s food scene is smaller and more vacation-focused than Bend’s, but it
          works well for casual family meals, coffee, groceries, pizza, patios, and easy
          dinners after a day outside.
        </p>

        <p>
          Many visitors also cook at their vacation rental, especially for longer stays.
          That is part of the Sunriver rhythm: breakfast at the house, bikes during the
          day, snacks between activities, and a casual dinner after everyone is tired.
        </p>

        <div class="callout">
          <strong>Helpful tip:</strong> During busy summer weeks and holiday periods,
          restaurants and grocery stops can get crowded. Planning simple meals at your
          rental can make the trip much easier.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Outdoor Recreation Near Sunriver</h2>
        <p>
          Sunriver has easy access to the Deschutes River, bike paths, golf courses,
          nearby trails, lava lands, lakes, forests, and winter routes toward Mt. Bachelor.
          It is a strong base for outdoor trips without staying directly in Bend.
        </p>

        <div class="grid">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Close to Sunriver</h3>
            <p>
              Bike paths, golf, river access, resort activities, nature areas, and family
              outings are all easy from town.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Nearby Outdoor Areas</h3>
            <p>
              Benham Falls, Lava Butte, Newberry National Volcanic Monument, La Pine
              State Park, and the Deschutes River are all nearby.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Mountain and Lake Trips</h3>
            <p>
              Mt. Bachelor, Cascade Lakes Highway, Elk Lake, Sparks Lake, and other
              mountain areas are common day trips.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Sunriver Areas and Nearby Places</h2>

        <div class="grid">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>The Village at Sunriver</h3>
